### Typography
**Adopted 2026-08-09 — two-font system** (`--font-display` / `--font-sans` in `src/index.css`):
- Display (`--font-display`): **Titillium Web** (400/600/700/900) — all headings (h1–h6), page/section
  titles, hero/marketing headline text, large numeric emphasis on metric cards.
- Body (`--font-sans`): **Rajdhani** (400/500/600/700) — everything else: body copy, nav links,
  labels, ALL interactive components (buttons, links styled as buttons, tabs, toggles, badges,
  chips), and all form inputs/selects/textareas.
- Mono (`--font-mono`): JetBrains Mono — reserved for **read-only** numeric/data display only
  (data table cells, computed-value readouts; tabular-figure alignment). As of 2026-08-10 this no
  longer includes form inputs — those moved to `--font-sans` alongside the rest of the
  interactive layer.
- Both loaded via Google Fonts `<link>` in `index.html`, same pattern as the existing JetBrains
  Mono load.
- Style: clean hierarchy, large numeric emphasis for metrics, open spacing

**Header weight/spacing (adopted 2026-08-10, ported from the main Authority OS site).** Heavy
display weights combined with negative letter-spacing and tight (1.05–1.1) line-height read as
cramped. Fix: move to positive tracking + slightly looser line-height, at two tiers —
- **Hero/primary headings** (page-level titles — `PanelHero` in `ui.jsx`, and the equivalent
  inline-styled 32–52px section openers in `HomePanel.jsx`/`IncomePanel.jsx`): `font-weight: 900`,
  `letter-spacing: 0.04em`, `line-height: 1.15`.
- **Secondary page headers** (section/modal titles — `SectionHeader` in `ui.jsx`, modal titles in
  `ChangelogModal`/`ConsentGateModal`/`LegalDocumentModal`, ProfilePanel's tax-section titles,
  HomePanel's "Year-End Outlook"): `font-weight: 800`, `letter-spacing: 0.02em`,
  `line-height: 1.15`.
- Em-based letter-spacing (not px) so tracking scales proportionally with font-size rather than
  staying fixed — matters most on mobile where header sizes shrink.
- Utility classes `.heading-xl` (700 / 0.04em / 1.15) and `.heading-lg` (800 / -0.02em / 1.25)
  added to `src/index.css` for parity with the main site's system — not yet referenced by any
  component here (A:Fin builds headers as inline styles / the `PanelHero`/`SectionHeader`
  components, not via a class system).

**Body-text size scale (adopted 2026-08-10, bumped +1px again 2026-08-11).** Non-numeric text —
labels, sublabels, descriptions, list summaries — MUST use one of five `text-*` utility classes
in `src/index.css` instead of a hardcoded inline `fontSize`, so the whole scale has one place to
tune instead of hundreds of scattered px literals:
- `.text-2xs` → 11px
- `.text-xs` → 12px
- `.text-sm` → 13px
- `.text-base` → 14px
- `.text-md` → 15px

Large numeric emphasis (MetricCard values, dollar totals, computed readouts) is explicitly out
of scope — it keeps whatever per-component sizing it already had.

**Migration status: complete (2026-08-10), enforced going forward.** Every component under
`src/components/` + `App.jsx` — all of `ui.jsx`'s shared primitives plus every panel, modal, and
lower-traffic surface — is converted; nothing left with a hardcoded inline `fontSize` in this
range except `Card`'s dynamic `size` prop (numeric, always exempt), a few dynamically-scaled
template-literal sizes, and 8 shared JS style objects (same DRY treatment as `ui.jsx`'s `lS` —
the object is the single source of truth for every render site that uses it). A static-analysis
test, `src/test/lib/textUtilityClassAudit.test.js`, greps every component file for raw
`fontSize: "Npx"` literals and fails `npm run test:run` the moment new code reintroduces one
outside that documented allowlist — see `docs/ux-animations-tasks.md`'s Typography section for
the full rollout history, the Tailwind name-collision gotcha (`.text-xs`/`.text-sm`/`.text-base`
share names with Tailwind's own defaults — never wrap the `.text-*` block in `@layer`), and the
exact allowlist.
- Header weight/tracking fix (§ above) is scoped to actual header/title text only — large
  *numeric* emphasis (MetricCard values, dollar totals, computed readouts) intentionally keeps
  its existing weight/tracking; that's data display, not headline text, and isn't part of
  either the header fix or the body-text scale.

### Component Style
- Cards: floating, rounded (12–16px), soft shadows, minimal borders
- Layout: grid-based, 12px gap, 20px section margins
- Spacing: more breathing room than dense dashboards

### Motion Rules
- Transitions: smooth, ease-in-out — motion feels like flow, not reward
- No bounce, no arcade effects, no scale-up on mount
- Press state: `scale(0.97)` only
- All durations ≤ 500ms (except countup at 1200ms)
- Entrance stagger: `fadeSlideUp` 400ms, 80ms/card delay, capped at 400ms

### What to Avoid
- neon green overload or Cash App clone feel
- loud gradients or banding
- overly flat design (needs depth)
- gamified motion or reward feedback
- rigid enterprise table layouts

